Do not build the x86-ansi stubs and plugins

NSIS unconditionally builds ANSI installer stubs and plugin variants
alongside the Unicode ones whenever the target CPU is x86, with no
option to disable them. ANSI installers are a legacy compatibility
format w64devkit does not need: makensis defaults to Unicode on every
target, and a script requesting "Target x86-ansi" fails cleanly with
"adequate stub not found". Dropping them keeps the x86 kit and the
multilib kit's secondary x86 stub set Unicode-only and identical in
shape to the amd64 set.

---
 SConstruct |    7 -------
 1 file changed, 7 deletions(-)

--- a/SConstruct
+++ b/SConstruct
@@ -697,11 +697,6 @@
 	if defenv['UNICODE']:
 		BuildStub(stub, False, True)
 		BuildStub(stub, True, True)
